    "narrative": "With the scarcity of stolen bases remaining the primary lever for LawDog, our lineup optimization for June 11 reflects a premium on contact and speed-inclusive profiles. **Geraldo Perdomo** secures the highest score of the active group at 56.039, bolstered by a favorable 4.33 xERA matchup against Phillips. While he lacks elite power, the combination of his spot in the batting order and the projection adjustment for his recent efficiency makes him our anchor. **Taylor Ward** trails closely at 52.713; despite the sub-optimal 3.42 xERA of Woo, **Taylor Ward** benefits significantly from a high-run-environment park adjustment (+16%) and a leadoff slot assignment that maximizes his potential for counting stats. **Masyn Winn** (50.763) continues to be a mandatory start for us; his ability to contribute to the SB category against Scott (4.08 xERA) provides a safe floor, even if the current park factors are slightly suppressive. **Gleyber Torres** (48.513) rounds out the group, though he remains the most volatile play today due to a negative platoon split against Matthews.\n\nThe bench decision process was lean today given the scheduled off-days for **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** and **Lawrence Butler**, alongside the confirmed IL stashes of **Cal Raleigh** and **Yainer Diaz**. Because our bench is devoid of active depth for this specific slate, the \"next man up\" logic remains hypothetical; however, if **Tyler Freeman**, **Bryson Stott**, or **Will Smith** were active, they would have easily eclipsed the marginal scores of **Gleyber Torres**. We are currently monitoring **Matt Chapman**, **Daulton Varsho**, and **Luis Arraez** for future rotation availability. For tonight, we are comfortable with our active quartet, though we remain wary of the strikeout potential of opposing starters like Woo. Barring any late-scratch lineup shuffles for **Masyn Winn** or **Geraldo Perdomo**, our strategy remains focused on maintaining category efficiency without over-extending our game cap usage on high-risk, low-reward platoon gambles involving **Dylan Beavers**, **Jonathan Aranda**, **Jeremiah Jackson**, **Brendan Donovan**, **Jung Hoo Lee**, **Gavin Sheets**, or **Drew Gilbert**.",
